/**
 * @file modules.dox
 *
 * Module groups of the Cuarzo Framework. Each library subproject is one
 * module; module-filter.py places the headers of subprojects/cz-<name> in
 * their module. The order of the groups here is the order of the module list.
 */

/**
@defgroup module_core Core
@brief Core classes and utilities shared by every Cuarzo library: objects, signals, events, timers, animations and logging.

<table class="cz-module-info">
<tr><th>Header</th><td><tt>\#include <CZ/Core/CZCore.h></tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>pkg-config</th><td><tt>cz-core</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Meson</th><td><tt>dependency('cz-core')</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Depends on</th><td>Skia</td></tr>
</table>

Core is the foundation of the framework. It provides the main event loop (@ref CZ::CZCore "CZCore"), the
object model every other library builds on (@ref CZ::CZObject "CZObject", @ref CZ::CZSignal "CZSignal", @ref CZ::CZWeak "CZWeak", CZOwn),
the input and window events delivered to applications and compositors, timers, animations and
the logger.

<h2 id="module_core_overview">Main Classes</h2>

- **Event loop**: @ref CZ::CZCore "CZCore" drives timers, file descriptor event sources (@ref CZ::CZEventSource "CZEventSource") and
  queued events. Applications create it once with `CZCore::GetOrMake()`.
- **Objects and signals**: @ref CZ::CZObject "CZObject", @ref CZ::CZSignal "CZSignal" and @ref CZ::CZListener "CZListener" for callbacks;
  @ref CZ::CZWeak "CZWeak" references that become `nullptr` when their object is destroyed.
- **Events**: input (pointer, keyboard, touch and gesture events), layout, window state,
  color scheme and presentation events, all deriving from @ref CZ::CZEvent "CZEvent".
- **Animations**: @ref CZ::CZAnimation "CZAnimation", @ref CZ::CZLinearAnimation "CZLinearAnimation" and @ref CZ::CZSpringAnimation "CZSpringAnimation".
- **D-Bus**: @ref CZ::CZBus "CZBus" connects to the system and user buses from the event loop;
  @ref CZ::CZBusWorker "CZBusWorker" runs blocking calls on a background thread and hands their results back to it.
- **Utilities**: CZTransform, @ref CZ::CZRRect "CZRRect", @ref CZ::CZBitset "CZBitset", @ref CZ::CZSpFd "CZSpFd", shared memory,
  string, math and region helpers.
*/

/**
@defgroup module_ream Ream
@brief Graphics library for Linux: GPU buffer allocation, DMA-buf sharing between devices and a portable painter.

<table class="cz-module-info">
<tr><th>Header</th><td><tt>\#include <CZ/Ream/RCore.h></tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>pkg-config</th><td><tt>cz-ream</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Meson</th><td><tt>dependency('cz-ream')</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Depends on</th><td>@ref module_core, Skia</td></tr>
</table>

Ream abstracts the platform (DRM, Wayland, offscreen) and the graphics API (OpenGL ES 2.0,
Vulkan, raster) behind one API. It allocates GPU buffers (native, GBM/DMA-buf or dumb buffers),
shares them across devices on hybrid GPU systems, synchronizes them with explicit `sync_file`
fences and draws into them with a built-in painter or with Skia.

<h2 id="module_ream_overview">Main Classes</h2>

- @ref CZ::RCore "RCore" initializes Ream for a platform and graphics API; get it anywhere with `RCore::Get()`.
- @ref CZ::RDevice "RDevice" represents a GPU. @ref CZ::RImage "RImage" is an image that can be shared across devices,
  @ref CZ::RSurface "RSurface" wraps an image to draw into, and @ref CZ::RPainter "RPainter" draws into it.
- Portable code uses the classes directly under `CZ/Ream`; API-specific implementations live
  in `CZ/Ream/GL`, `CZ/Ream/VK` and `CZ/Ream/RS` (reached with e.g. `image->asGL()`).

See @ref abstraction_page for how the platform and API abstraction works.
*/

/**
@defgroup module_srm SRM
@brief Simple Rendering Manager: DRM/KMS display output with multi-GPU support.

<table class="cz-module-info">
<tr><th>Header</th><td><tt>\#include <CZ/SRM/SRMCore.h></tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>pkg-config</th><td><tt>cz-srm</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Meson</th><td><tt>dependency('cz-srm')</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Depends on</th><td>@ref module_core, @ref module_ream</td></tr>
</table>

SRM finds the DRM devices and connectors of the system, picks the best GPU to render each
connector, and handles mode setting, page flipping, cursor planes, direct scanout, gamma and
DRM leases. You render each connector's frames with Ream from the callbacks of a
SRMConnectorInterface.

<h2 id="module_srm_overview">Main Classes</h2>

- @ref CZ::SRMCore "SRMCore" enumerates @ref CZ::SRMDevice "SRMDevice" objects (GPUs), each with its connectors, CRTCs, encoders
  and planes.
- @ref CZ::SRMConnector "SRMConnector" is a display output; `initialize()` starts its rendering thread and calls
  your SRMConnectorInterface to draw each frame.
- @ref CZ::SRMLease "SRMLease" leases connectors to other clients (e.g. VR headsets).
*/

/**
@defgroup module_louvre Louvre
@brief Library for building Wayland compositors.

<table class="cz-module-info">
<tr><th>Header</th><td><tt>\#include <CZ/Louvre/LCompositor.h></tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>pkg-config</th><td><tt>cz-louvre</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Meson</th><td><tt>dependency('cz-louvre')</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Depends on</th><td>@ref module_core, @ref module_ream, @ref module_srm, Skia</td></tr>
</table>

Louvre uses the factory method pattern to provide default implementations for all major
functionality and protocols, which you override gradually: a compositor works from day one and
you customize it class by class. It handles the DRM and Wayland backends, input through
libinput, buffer management, explicit synchronization, fractional scaling, multi-GPU setups and
around forty Wayland protocols.

<h2 id="module_louvre_overview">Main Classes</h2>

- @ref CZ::LCompositor "LCompositor" is the entry point; override its `createObjectRequest()` to return your own
  subclasses of the factory objects (@ref CZ::LFactoryObject "LFactoryObject").
- @ref CZ::LSurface "LSurface", @ref CZ::LToplevelRole "LToplevelRole", @ref CZ::LPopupRole "LPopupRole", @ref CZ::LLayerRole "LLayerRole" and the other roles
  represent client windows.
- @ref CZ::LOutput "LOutput" is a display, @ref CZ::LSeat "LSeat" with @ref CZ::LPointer "LPointer", @ref CZ::LKeyboard "LKeyboard" and @ref CZ::LTouch "LTouch" handles
  input, and @ref CZ::LClient "LClient" is a connected client.
*/

/**
@defgroup module_kay Kay
@brief GPU-accelerated GUI toolkit: a scene of nodes laid out with Yoga and drawn with Skia or Ream.

<table class="cz-module-info">
<tr><th>Header</th><td><tt>\#include <CZ/AK/AKScene.h></tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>pkg-config</th><td><tt>cz-kay</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Meson</th><td><tt>dependency('cz-kay')</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Depends on</th><td>@ref module_core, @ref module_ream, @ref module_asset_broker, Skia, Yoga</td></tr>
</table>

Kay builds user interfaces from trees of nodes. Scenes track damage so only changed regions
are drawn again, support fractional scaling and screen transforms, and can be embedded in
Wayland clients (through @ref module_marco) or in compositors.

<h2 id="module_kay_overview">Main Classes</h2>

- @ref CZ::AKScene "AKScene" is a node tree; @ref CZ::AKTarget "AKTarget" defines how and where it's drawn.
- @ref CZ::AKNode "AKNode" is the base of every node: @ref CZ::AKContainer "AKContainer" only lays out its children,
  @ref CZ::AKRenderable "AKRenderable" draws directly, @ref CZ::AKBakeable "AKBakeable" draws into a cached image and @ref CZ::AKSubScene "AKSubScene"
  renders its children into its own image.
- Ready to use components: buttons (@ref CZ::AKButton "AKButton", @ref CZ::AKIconButton "AKIconButton"), drop-down lists (@ref CZ::AKPopUpButton "AKPopUpButton"), switches
  (@ref CZ::AKSwitch "AKSwitch"), check boxes (@ref CZ::AKCheckBox "AKCheckBox"), segmented controls
  (@ref CZ::AKSegmentedControl "AKSegmentedControl"), sliders (@ref CZ::AKSlider "AKSlider"), level meters
  (@ref CZ::AKLevelIndicator "AKLevelIndicator"), text fields (@ref CZ::AKTextInput "AKTextInput", @ref CZ::AKSearchField "AKSearchField",
  @ref CZ::AKCoreTextEditor "AKCoreTextEditor"), settings forms (@ref CZ::AKFormSection "AKFormSection" with
  @ref CZ::AKFormRow "AKFormRow" rows), sidebars (@ref CZ::AKSidebarList "AKSidebarList", @ref CZ::AKSidebarItem "AKSidebarItem"),
  icons (@ref CZ::AKFontIcon "AKFontIcon", @ref CZ::AKIconTile "AKIconTile", @ref CZ::AKWiFiIcon "AKWiFiIcon"),
  @ref CZ::AKAvatar "AKAvatar", @ref CZ::AKActivityIndicator "AKActivityIndicator", scroll views (@ref CZ::AKScroll "AKScroll"),
  images, and background effects such as shadows and blur.

Guides: @ref core_components_page, @ref creating_components_page and @ref events_page.
*/

/**
@defgroup module_marco Marco
@brief Library for building Wayland applications with Kay.

<table class="cz-module-info">
<tr><th>Header</th><td><tt>\#include <CZ/Marco/MApp.h></tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>pkg-config</th><td><tt>cz-marco</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Meson</th><td><tt>dependency('cz-marco')</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Depends on</th><td>@ref module_core, @ref module_ream, @ref module_kay, @ref module_xdgkit, Skia</td></tr>
</table>

Marco connects to the Wayland compositor, creates the Ream context and gives each surface a Kay
scene, so windows, popups and panels are built with Kay nodes.

<h2 id="module_marco_overview">Main Classes</h2>

- @ref CZ::MApp "MApp" is the application; @ref CZ::MScreen "MScreen" represents an output.
- Surface roles: @ref CZ::MToplevel "MToplevel" (windows), @ref CZ::MDialog "MDialog" (dialogs attached to a window),
  @ref CZ::MPopup "MPopup" and @ref CZ::MMenu "MMenu", @ref CZ::MTooltip "MTooltip",
  @ref CZ::MSubsurface "MSubsurface", @ref CZ::MLayerSurface "MLayerSurface" (`wlr_layer_shell` panels and backgrounds) and
  @ref CZ::MSessionLockSurface "MSessionLockSurface".
- Nodes: @ref CZ::MVibrancyView "MVibrancyView" (blurred backgrounds), @ref CZ::MSidebar "MSidebar" (a resizable window
  sidebar with the window buttons), @ref CZ::MPopUpButton "MPopUpButton" (a drop-down list opening an MMenu) and the menu
  items (@ref CZ::MMenuView "MMenuView", @ref CZ::MMenuAction "MMenuAction").
- Extensions for desktop components: foreign toplevel management (@ref CZ::MForeignToplevelManager "MForeignToplevelManager"),
  output management (@ref CZ::MOutputManager "MOutputManager") and session locking.
*/

/**
@defgroup module_xdgkit XDGKit
@brief Utilities for the XDG specifications: icon themes, desktop entries, MIME types and the trash.

<table class="cz-module-info">
<tr><th>Header</th><td><tt>\#include <CZ/XDG/XDGKit.h></tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>pkg-config</th><td><tt>cz-xdgkit</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Meson</th><td><tt>dependency('cz-xdgkit')</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Depends on</th><td>@ref module_core</td></tr>
</table>

@ref CZ::XDGKit "XDGKit" finds icons following the
[XDG Icon Theme Specification](https://specifications.freedesktop.org/icon-theme-spec/latest/),
using caches generated by `cz-xdgkit-icon-theme-indexer` for fast lookups. It doesn't load
icons: it returns their paths, sizes and formats. It also reads desktop entries, the MIME
database and the trash.

<h2 id="module_xdgkit_overview">Main Classes</h2>

- @ref CZ::XDGKit "XDGKit" is the entry point; @ref CZ::XDGIconThemeManager "XDGIconThemeManager" finds a @ref CZ::XDGIcon "XDGIcon" by name, size,
  scale and theme.
- @ref CZ::XDGDesktopEntry "XDGDesktopEntry", @ref CZ::XDGMimeDatabase "XDGMimeDatabase" and @ref CZ::XDGTrash "XDGTrash".
- Helper functions in the @ref CZ::XDGUtils "XDGUtils" namespace.
*/

/**
@defgroup module_services Services
@brief Clients of the system and session services a desktop shell needs: Wi-Fi, audio, status indicators, media players and notifications.

<table class="cz-module-info">
<tr><th>Header</th><td><tt>\#include <CZ/Services/SVWiFi.h></tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>pkg-config</th><td><tt>cz-services</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Meson</th><td><tt>dependency('cz-services')</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Depends on</th><td>@ref module_core, libsystemd (sd-bus)</td></tr>
</table>

Each service is a class of its own, independent from the others: it talks to its service over
D-Bus off the UI thread (see @ref CZ::CZBusWorker "CZBusWorker") and tells when its state changed
with signals. Without the service (or its hardware) its state says it isn't available.

Like @ref CZ::CZCore "CZCore", each one is shared by the process: `GetOrMake()` returns the instance
(made on first use), which lives while some shared pointer to it does.

<h2 id="module_services_overview">Main Classes</h2>

- @ref CZ::SVWiFi "SVWiFi": NetworkManager's Wi-Fi. Turning it on and off, the networks in range
  (@ref CZ::SVWiFiNetwork "SVWiFiNetwork"), joining (asking for passwords), forgetting them and their Auto-Join.
- @ref CZ::SVAudio "SVAudio": the audio devices of PipeWire or PulseAudio. The default output and input, or just
  some of their channels (@ref CZ::SVAudioSelection "SVAudioSelection"), their volume, the input level and playing sounds.
- @ref CZ::SVStatus "SVStatus": the network, volume and battery state as symbolic icon names, for a bar's indicators.
- @ref CZ::SVNowPlaying "SVNowPlaying": what MPRIS media players are playing, and controlling them.
- @ref CZ::SVNotificationsClient "SVNotificationsClient" sends desktop notifications (@ref CZ::SVNotification "SVNotification") and controls
  Gazette; @ref CZ::SVNotificationsServer "SVNotificationsServer" is the protocol side of a notifications daemon.
*/

/**
@defgroup module_heaven Heaven
@brief Global menus for Wayland sessions over D-Bus.

<table class="cz-module-info">
<tr><th>Headers</th><td><tt>\#include <CZ/Heaven/Bar/HNBar.h></tt><br><tt>\#include <CZ/Heaven/Client/HNClient.h></tt><br><tt>\#include <CZ/Heaven/Compositor/HNCompositor.h></tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>pkg-config</th><td><tt>cz-heaven-bar</tt>, <tt>cz-heaven-client</tt>, <tt>cz-heaven-compositor</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Meson</th><td><tt>dependency('cz-heaven-client')</tt> (etc.)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Depends on</th><td>@ref module_core</td></tr>
</table>

Heaven lets Wayland clients export their application menus to a single global menu application
(the bar), and lets the compositor decide whose menu is shown. The objects and their properties
are mirrored on both ends over the D-Bus session bus.

Heaven is three independent libraries, one for each side:

| Library | Used by | Role |
|---|---|---|
| @ref module_heaven_bar | The global menu application | Receives and mirrors the menus of every client; delivers clicks back. |
| @ref module_heaven_client | Applications | Publishes the app's menu tree and reacts to clicks. |
| @ref module_heaven_compositor | The compositor | Authenticates clients and tells the bar which one is active. |
*/

/**
@defgroup module_heaven_bar Heaven Bar
@ingroup module_heaven
@brief `cz-heaven-bar`: the global menu application's side (namespace `Bar`).
*/

/**
@defgroup module_heaven_client Heaven Client
@ingroup module_heaven
@brief `cz-heaven-client`: the application's side (namespace `Client`).
*/

/**
@defgroup module_heaven_compositor Heaven Compositor
@ingroup module_heaven
@brief `cz-heaven-compositor`: the compositor's side (namespace `Compositor`).
*/

/**
@defgroup module_asset_broker AssetBroker
@brief Icon and image loading shared between apps as DMA-bufs.

<table class="cz-module-info">
<tr><th>Header</th><td><tt>\#include <CZ/AssetBroker/ABCore.h></tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>pkg-config</th><td><tt>cz-asset-broker</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Meson</th><td><tt>dependency('cz-asset-broker')</tt></td></tr>
<tr><th>Depends on</th><td>@ref module_core, @ref module_ream, @ref module_xdgkit</td></tr>
</table>

Assets (icons, SVGs and images) are either generated in each app or, when the `cz-asset-broker`
service is running, generated once by the service and shared with every app as DMA-bufs, so apps
use the same GPU buffers. Requesting the same icon, size and device again returns the same
@ref CZ::RImage "RImage" while some copy of it is alive.

<h2 id="module_asset_broker_overview">Main Classes</h2>

- @ref CZ::ABCore "ABCore" loads icons (described by a @ref CZ::ABIconKey "ABIconKey") and images, in-process or through the
  service depending on its mode (`ABMode::Auto`, `Local` or `Remote`).
- `ABCore::IconProvider()` plugs icons into Kay's image nodes.
- @ref CZ::ABServer "ABServer" is the service; the @ref CZ::ABProtocol "ABProtocol" namespace documents its wire protocol, and
  ABGenerators the assets it can generate.
*/
